From: OpenWrt RTL819x porting
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: untag VID 0 on the RTL8197F 4-byte-tag conduit

The RTL8197F MAC forces the switch's 4-byte hardware CPU tag, which cannot
carry the DSA tag's KEEP bit. CPU-injected frames are therefore seen as tagged
by the switch and, because the CPU port has no PVID, classified into VID 0.
With VLAN filtering disabled the driver selected REAL_KEEP, so every
router-originated frame egressed with an 802.1Q priority tag (TPID 0x8100,
VID 0) on all LAN and WAN ports.

Always follow the VLAN4k untag mask (ORIGINAL) and program VID 0 as member +
untagged on every available port. DSA reserves VID 0 and never programs it, so
the entry does not conflict with the VLAN/MC bookkeeping; unprogrammed VIDs
keep untag=0 and preserve tagged passthrough.

Tested on a Knup KP-RW407/AX: LAN and WAN captures no longer show 0x8100 on
router-originated unicast, broadcast or multicast; VLAN-aware bridges are
unaffected.

---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_main.c
@@ -1991,14 +1991,16 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* When VLAN filtering is disabled, preserve frames exactly as received.
-	 * Otherwise, the VLAN egress pipeline may still alter tag state
-	 * according to VLAN membership and untag configuration.
+	/* The RTL8197F conduit forces the 4-byte hardware CPU tag, which
+	 * cannot carry the DSA tag's KEEP bit: CPU-injected frames are seen as
+	 * tagged and, with no CPU PVID, classified into VID 0. Always follow
+	 * the VLAN4k untag mask so VID 0 can be made untagged (see
+	 * rtl8365mb_vlan_setup). With filtering enabled this is unchanged;
+	 * with filtering disabled DSA still programs the bridge VLANs, so
+	 * untagged bridge traffic keeps its format and unprogrammed VIDs keep
+	 * untag=0, preserving tagged passthrough.
 	 */
-	if (vlan_filtering)
-		mode = RTL8365MB_VLAN_EGRESS_MODE_ORIGINAL;
-	else
-		mode = RTL8365MB_VLAN_EGRESS_MODE_REAL_KEEP;
+	mode = RTL8365MB_VLAN_EGRESS_MODE_ORIGINAL;
 
 	ret = rtl8365mb_port_set_vlan_egress_mode(priv, port, mode);
 	if (ret)
@@ -2134,9 +2136,13 @@
  */
 static int rtl8365mb_vlan_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 {
+	struct switchdev_obj_port_vlan vlan0 = {
+		.vid = 0,
+		.flags = BRIDGE_VLAN_INFO_UNTAGGED,
+	};
 	struct realtek_priv *priv = ds->priv;
 	struct dsa_port *dp;
-	int ret;
+	int ret = 0;
 
 	dsa_switch_for_each_available_port(dp, ds) {
 		/* Disable vlan-filtering for all ports */
@@ -2149,6 +2155,27 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* The 4-byte hardware CPU tag cannot carry the DSA tag's KEEP bit.
+	 * Frames injected by the CPU are therefore treated as tagged and,
+	 * because the CPU port has no PVID, classified into VID 0. Program
+	 * VID 0 as member + untagged on every available port so the egress
+	 * pipeline cannot add a priority tag (802.1Q, VID 0) to them. DSA
+	 * never programs VID 0 (it is reserved), so this does not conflict
+	 * with the VLAN/MC bookkeeping.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&priv->vlan_lock);
+	dsa_switch_for_each_available_port(dp, ds) {
+		ret = rtl8365mb_vlan_4k_port_add(ds, dp->index, &vlan0, NULL);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(priv->dev, "Failed to program VLAN 0 on port %d\n",
+				dp->index);
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&priv->vlan_lock);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	/* VLAN is always enabled. */
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(priv->map, RTL8365MB_VLAN_CTRL_REG,
 				 RTL8365MB_VLAN_CTRL_EN_MASK,
